    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=9553338f-c93c-40ce-9a23-04b38f1294de&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201097293221_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Biological Principles",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-07\n\nLocation: Newburgh\n\nAdjunct Faculty Position for Biological Principles The Natural Sciences Division at Mount Saint Mary College seeks qualified individuals to teach Biological Principles I lab.  This course is the first of a two-course introductory biology sequence for science majors emphasizing the chemical and cellular basis of life.  Lab activities involve inquiry-based experiments, data analysis, and student presentations.  Previously developed lab modules will be available for use.  This course is offered during the traditional 15-week semester schedule.  Qualifications include : A Master’s degree or higher is required in biology or a related field, or in education.  Previous teaching experience is preferred.  Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis.  All offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Compensation: Compensation: $660-$780 per credit If interested, please submit letter of application and include a resume/curriculum vitae and two letters of recommendation.   Mount Saint Mary College is a Catholic, Dominican liberal arts college located in New York’s scenic Hudson Valley, 60 miles north of New York City. Preparing students for personal and professional success, the College offers bachelor’s and master’s degree programs in healthcare, business, education, social services, communication and media, the liberal arts, and more.",
