    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=9553338f-c93c-40ce-9a23-04b38f1294de&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201202579289_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor for Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-07\n\nLocation: Newburgh\n\nJob Title : Adjunct Instructor for Chemistry Reports To : Chair, Natural Science Status : Contract, Part-Time  The Division of Natural Sciences at Mount Saint Mary College (Newburgh, NY) seeks qualified individuals to teach one or more sections of Nursing Chemistry Fundamentals, beginning Fall 2026, but also with the possibility of an ongoing basis. This course introduces nursing students to the basic concepts of general, organic, and biochemistry specifically as they apply to the life sciences. The 3-hour laboratory scheduled for the course will include one hour of recitation, which incorporates problem solving and the quantitative aspects of chemical behavior, along with 2 hours of hands-on laboratory work. Previously-developed materials are available for use. This course is offered during the traditional 15-week semester schedule, from late-August through mid-December. Primary Duties and Responsibilities   Provide support and guidance to students Instruct an assigned course, providing syllabi and other instructional materials Use of College learning management systems to deliver instruction Prepare and deliver course materials (lectures, labs, assignments, assessments) in alignment with departmental learning goals. Maintain course records, grade assignments, and submit final grades in a timely manner. Provide students with regular feedback on performance and be available during office hours or by appointment. Adhere to departmental and college policies and deadlines. Coordinate with course coordinators and laboratory staff as needed   Knowledge, skills, and abilities   Must have computer skills to include knowledgeable use of Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, and PowerPoint). Show proficiency in oral and written communications with the ability to generate high-quality classroom materials. Demonstrate the ability to clearly and engagingly present information, lead class activities, and facilitate student learning. Have leadership abilities to guide students in hands-on, design, or technology management in the laboratory setting. Demonstrate commitment to student success and academic excellence.   Requirements   A graduate degree in Chemistry or a related field. Demonstrated experience within the field of Chemistry. Physical and Other Requirements   May require standing for long periods of time May require talking for long periods of time May require carrying course materials   Modality:   In-person only   Additional Materials and Procedure Letter summarizing your interest in and qualifications for the position. Official transcripts from all graduate-level institutions at which the candidate studied and/or from which the candidate obtained a degree. Current curriculum vitae that includes evidence of teaching experience and effectiveness, as well as courses developed and/or taught. Two letters of professional reference. Compensation $2490-3450, depending on degree and lecture/lab taught Review of applications will begin immediately. For information about Mount Saint Mary College, please visit www.msmc.edu . Questions about this position can be forwarded to douglas.robinson@msmc.edu , Chair – Division of Natural Sciences Program for the School of Art, Sciences, and Education.    Mount Saint Mary College is an independent liberal arts college located in New York’s scenic Hudson Valley, 60 miles north of New York City, with a strong focus on preparing students for lifelong service. The College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer with a strong commitment to diversifying its faculty and staff. Mount Saint Mary College does not discriminate in its employment, operations, programs, and services on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, age, disability, marital status, citizenship, national origin, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by law.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=9553338f-c93c-40ce-9a23-04b38f1294de&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201207809969_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "CRM and Operations Specialist (Onsite)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-07\n\nLocation: Newburgh\n\nJob Title: CRM and Operations Specialist  Reports To: Associate Director of Admission Status: Full-Time, Exempt  Modality: In-person (On-Campus) Summary/objective Reporting to the Associate Director of Admissions, the CRM and Operations Specialist supports the Admissions office with the execution, auditing, planning, process review, and the evaluation of all aspects related to initiating and completing applications for the Admissions Office. This position will also assist with the maintenance, monitoring, and improvement of the CRM (Slate) functions. This is an on-campus position.  Essential functions Serve as an administrator for the Slate CRM, managing system configuration, maintenance, optimization, and ongoing enhancements in support of undergraduate admissions operations.  Design, build, and maintain Slate functionality including applications, forms, portals, reader workflows, communication plans, configurable joins, datasets, queries, reports, rules, permissions, and automations.  Lead the continuous assessment and optimization of Slate functionality by researching new features, best practices, and system enhancements to maximize platform capabilities.  Develop and maintain data integrations between Slate, the Student Information System (Jenzabar), Axiom, testing vendors, financial aid systems, and other third-party applications while ensuring data integrity and accuracy.  Monitor, troubleshoot, and resolve complex system, integration, and data issues across Slate and related enterprise systems.  Establish and maintain data governance standards through regular auditing, validation, duplicate management, and reconciliation of admissions and enrollment data.  Manage the import and validation of prospect, applicant, and testing data including purchased search names, SAT/ACT, AP, Common App, and other external data sources.  Build and maintain advanced reporting and dashboards that support operational decision-making, enrollment management, and institutional reporting.  Collaborate with Information Technology, Financial Aid, Registrar, and Enrollment leadership on system enhancements, integrations, and strategic initiatives.  Oversee applicant-facing Slate functionality, including the applicant portal, ensuring an intuitive and effective user experience while resolving escalated technical issues.  Manage and optimize document management processes, application review workflows, and electronic records to ensure efficient processing and compliance.  Configure and maintain financial aid data imports and related applicant communications within Slate.  Develop documentation, standard operating procedures, and training materials for Slate users across the admissions team.  Provide functional training, and ongoing support for admissions staff, promoting effective use of Slate and adoption of best practices.  Recommend and implement process improvements through automation, workflow redesign, and emerging technologies.  Participate in recruitment and yield activities (e.g. open houses, information sessions, admitted student programs) as needed.  Perform other duties as assigned. Skills/Abilities Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with high attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to train team members on CRM functions and proper use. Ability to collaborate effectively across departments and functional areas. Proficiency with Microsoft Excel and Word. Accurate and efficient data input skills with an eye for detail. Comfortable learning and adapting to new   technologies and software. Experience working in a highly collaborative diverse environment with the ability to maintain confidentiality of data. Participate in on campus recruitment and yield events, including but not limited to Open Houses, Information Sessions, and Accepted Student Days. Maintain a broad knowledge base about the College, its programs and opportunities. Maintain broad knowledge base about general trends in secondary and higher education.   Supervisory responsibilities  This position has no supervisory responsibilities or direct reports. Work environment Office Setting: Cubicles, open desks, or private offices with access to necessary tools like computers, phones, and office supplies. Remote Setting: Working from home or another location with access to virtual communication platforms and necessary technology.   Physical demands Sitting: Ability to remain in a stationary position and operate a computer for extended periods. Typing/Computer Use: Frequent use of a computer keyboard and mouse. Vision Requirements: Ability to read and view screens for extended periods. Speaking/Hearing: Regular communication with coworkers and clients in person, over the phone, or via video calls. Lifting/Carrying: Occasionally lifting or moving items/boxes up to 40 pounds. Reaching/Bending: Periodic reaching for or bending to access files, supplies, or equipment. Mobility: Walking short distances within the office or to meeting rooms. Schedule requirement Occasional evening and weekend work to support recruitment events. Required education and experience Bachelor’s degree. Minimum of 2 years of experience in Higher education, admissions, or Slate/data operations. Experience working in a Slate or admissions/enrollment technology platform. Demonstrated experience managing data, processes, and systems in a complex, collaborative environment.   Work authorization/security clearance requirements Must be authorized to work in the United States. MSMC does not sponsor employment visas at this time. EEO statement Mount Saint Mary College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. We actively encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.   Other duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=9553338f-c93c-40ce-9a23-04b38f1294de&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201110908288_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Security Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-06\n\nLocation: Newburgh\n\nJob Title: Security Officer Reports To: Director of Security and Safety Status:  Full-Time, Non-Exempt  Summary/objective The Security Officer is responsible for maintaining a safe and secure campus environment through proactive patrol, response to incidents, and engagement with the campus community. This role supports the safety of students, faculty, staff, and visitors by enforcing college policies, responding to emergencies, and providing excellent customer service. Essential functions Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform these essential functions. Provide general campus security through vehicle patrol, foot patrol, and fixed post assignments.  Respond to alarms, calls for service, and emergency situations in a timely manner.  Detect, deter, and investigate unusual or suspicious activity.  Provide information, assistance, and support to students, employees, and visitors.  Observe and report violations of campus policies and applicable laws.  Enforce college regulations, including motor vehicle and parking policies.  Complete clear, accurate, and timely security incident reports.  Deliver excellent customer service in all interactions.  Provide first aid as needed, including use of AED and administering CPR.  Respond to assignments as directed by dispatch or supervisory personnel.  Identify, document, and report unsafe conditions; take corrective action when possible.  Perform dispatching duties as assigned, including:  Answering incoming calls  Monitoring cameras, access control, and fire systems  Monitoring radio communications  Maintaining accountability for department property  Perform additional safety and security functions as directed.  Supervisory responsibilities  The position of security officer does not have any direct reports. Work environment Outdoor and indoor campus environment, including patrol of buildings, parking lots, and roadways.  Exposure to varying weather conditions during patrol duties.  Work may include evenings, nights, weekends, and holidays.  Occasional high-stress situations requiring quick decision-making. Physical demands Extensive walking and standing for prolonged periods during foot patrols across campus, including buildings, stairwells, parking lots, and roadways.  Ability to climb stairs, navigate uneven terrain, and move quickly between locations.  Ability to respond rapidly to emergency situations, which may include running, bending, kneeling, or crouching.  Ability to move 75 pounds and lift 40 pounds when necessary.  Frequent use of hands for operating radios, computers, and other security equipment.  Visual and auditory acuity sufficient to observe surroundings, monitor security systems, and respond to alarms and incidents.  Ability to work in varying environmental conditions, including outdoor weather extremes such as heat, cold, rain, or snow. Travel required  The security officer position doesn’t require travel other than local movement throughout campus. Required education and experience High school diploma or GED Minimum of two (2) years of experience as a security officer, police officer, firefighter, or related field  Ability to read, write, and communicate effectively in order to complete reports, understand instructions, and respond to emergency situations Valid New York State driver’s license  Current New York State security guard certification  Ability to work independently with minimal supervision  Basic computer skills, including email, report writing systems, and online training platforms  Ability to effectively respond to emergency situations with urgency and sound judgment Preferred education and experience Some college coursework or military experience  Prior experience in a higher education or campus setting  CPR/AED certification  Benefits Medical Dental Vision 403(b) Retirement Plan (Pre-Tax & Roth Options) 403(b) Employer Match  Generous Paid Time Off Paid Holidays EAP Voluntary Life Voluntary AD&D Voluntary Hospital Insurance Voluntary Critical Illness Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts – Health, Dependent Care College Paid Life Insurance College Paid Long Term Disability Tuition Remission – Self and Dependents  Tuition Exchange Program Work authorization/security clearance requirements Must be authorized to work in the United States. MSMC does not sponsor employment visas at this time. EEO statement Mount Saint Mary College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. We actively encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.   Other duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice.             \n Available shift: 12:00 AM-8:00 AM",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=9553338f-c93c-40ce-9a23-04b38f1294de&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201006808020_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Instructor/Assistant Professor/Associate Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-22\n\nLocation: Newburgh\n\nJob Title:         Instructor/Assistant Professor/Associate Professor of Nursing          Reports To:     Dean, School of Nursing Status:             Full-Time, Exempt      The Mount Saint Mary College School of Nursing seeks full-time, tenure-track and/or non-tenure track nursing faculty members to join our CCNE-accredited program dedicated to educating the next generation of nurses.  Our faculty work closely with undergraduate and graduate students through teaching in the classroom, skills laboratories, simulation labs, and/or clinical settings. Additionally, faculty will have the opportunity to advise nursing students, participate in curriculum and program development, and perform other academic duties in accordance with the mission and purpose of Mount Saint Mary College and the School of Nursing. Tenure-track positions also include expectations of scholarship for promotion. Exceptional candidates may be granted service time towards promotion and/or tenure.   The successful candidate will: Demonstrate a commitment to effective teaching and mentoring students, to guide student learning in the pre-licensure and graduate nursing programs; Assist with course coordination and supervision of clinical adjunct faculty in accordance with course requirements; Work collaboratively with faculty in program planning, curriculum construction or revision, and fulfillment of accreditation requirements for the School of Nursing;  Provide academic advising to students to assist in degree completion and job placement; Participate in the School of Nursing and College academic committees; Actively engage in College-wide activities such as Open Houses, Admitted Students Day, Faculty Development Days, and Commencement; Be responsive to student needs through availability for office hours and on campus days; Demonstrate a strong commitment to work with a diverse group of undergraduate and graduate nursing students, especially first-generation students.     Required Qualifications:  Master's degree in Nursing from an accredited college or university; At least five (5) years of clinical experience; Unencumbered current New York RN license or eligibility.    Preferred Qualifications:   Doctorate degree in Nursing or related field (Candidates enrolled in a doctoral program are invited to apply.) Experience in Nursing higher education in the classroom, laboratory, and/or clinic. Experience in Medical-Surgical, Critical Care, Mother Baby, Pediatrics, or Mental Health areas.   In addition to the employment application, candidates should submit: 1) a letter of interest detailing qualifications for the position; 2) their most recent CV; and 3) the names and contact information for three professional references.   About the Mount Saint Mary College School of Nursing:   Mount Saint Mary College School of Nursing prepares nurses with the Dominican values of spirituality, study, community, and service. Students engage in service learning to understand the social determinants of health and to promote social justice; use reflective practice and clinical judgement to provide compassionate, skilled, holistic care while respecting diversity, equity, and inclusion of all people; and are prepared to engage in life-long learning and to advance professional nursing practice.  The Mount Saint Mary College School of Nursing offers undergraduate BSN and RN-to-BSN degrees, master’s degrees in multiple Nurse Practitioner programs, a master’s degree in Nursing Education, and multiple post-master’s certificates.    About the Institution:  Mount Saint Mary College is a small, vibrant liberal arts college in a beautiful location overlooking the Hudson River.  The Mount is dedicated to the Dominican tradition of education that values the inherent worth of the individual, the mission of Mount Saint Mary College is to create an environment which fosters close student-faculty interaction that enables students to reach their full potential as lifelong learners. Mount Saint Mary College strives to provide a stimulating environment that promotes the intellectual and personal growth of undergraduate and graduate students.   Salary and Benefits: Faculty rank and salary will be commensurate with education and qualification.   Mount Saint Mary College is an equal-opportunity employer.",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
